@startuml clock-budget
!include common.iuml
left to right direction
title Clock budget controller, 1 move

component "Side to move\nbank = remaining, moves played = n" as side
component "Budget draw\nidempotent per move" as draw
component "Feedforward\nspendable = max(0, remaining - SearchSafetyMarginMs),\nmovesLeft = max(1, ClockExpectedMovesPerSide - n),\nfeedforward = spendable / movesLeft\n+ increment x ClockIncrementShare" as ff
component "PID controller\nerror = remaining - target,\ntarget = drain trajectory floored at SearchSafetyMarginMs,\ncorrection = clamp(pid(error),\n+ or - ClockPIDClampFraction x feedforward)" as pid
component "Grant\nclamp(feedforward + correction,\nSearchMinMoveTimeMs, max(spendable, SearchMinMoveTimeMs))" as grant
component "Search\nruns on the grant" as search
component "Commit\nremaining = max(0, remaining - elapsed) + increment,\nn = n + 1, the next move draws a fresh budget" as commit

side --> draw
draw --> ff
ff --> pid
pid --> grant
grant --> search
search --> commit
commit --> draw : Game continues
note bottom of grant
  The floor wins over the reserve: a fully drained 1+0
  clock still funds SearchMinMoveTimeMs moves, remaining
  never goes negative, a timeout can never decide a game
end note
@enduml
